istory (first round), use stratified random selection\n    # Mix of random and alphabetically diverse genes\n    if not history:\n        # Sort available indices by gene name for diversity\n        available_with_names = [(idx, candidates[idx].get(\'gene\', \'\')) for idx in available_indices]\n        available_with_names.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n        \n        # Select every nth gene to ensure diversity across the alphabet\n        if len(available_with_names) <= batch_size:\n            selected = [idx for idx, _ in available_with_names]\n        else:\n            step = len(available_with_names) / batch_size\n            selected = [available_with_names[int(i * step)][0] for i in range(batch_size)]'}
