evale22_Adenosine/run-2/best/current/harness/model.py"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_d487c51d1870490f822fede0', 'content': '{\n  "content": "  1| from __future__ import annotations\\n  2| \\n  3| def select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]:\\n  4|     \\"\\"\\"\\n  5|     Selection policy for Project-BDA.\\n  6| \\n  7|     Contract (MUST KEEP EXACTLY):\\n  8|         select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]\\n  9| \\n 10|     Inputs:\\n 11|     - candidates: list[dict]\\n 12|         - single-gene datasets: each item includes {\\"gene\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 13|         - gene-pair datasets: each item includes {\\"gene_a\\": \\"<HGNC>\\", \\"gene_b\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 14|         - gene search (optional): when enabled by the runner, you may call:\\n 15|           - import bda_tools\\n 16|           - bda_tools.gene_search(query_gene: str, k: int = 10, diverse: bool = False) -> list[int]\\n 17|     - history: list[dict]\\n 18|         - each item includes at least:\\n 19|           - candidate_index: int\\n 20|           - score: float\\n 21|           - hit: int (0/1) if enabled by runner\\n 22|     - batch_size: int\\n 23|     - seed: int\\n 24| \\n 25|     Output:\\n 26|     - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 27| \\n 28|     You may implement any suitable algorithmic model here, including but not limited to:\\n 29|     traditional algorithms, machine learning models, deep learning models, biological models,\\n 30|     and mathematical models.\\n 31|     \\"\\"\\"\\n 32|     import numpy as np\\n 33|     \\n 34|     # Set random seed for reproducibility\\n 35|     rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\\n 36|     \\n 37|     # Get all candidate indices\\n 38|     n_candidates = len(candidates)\\n 39|     candidate_indices = list(range(n_candidates))\\n 40|     \\n 41|     # Remove already selected candidates\\n 42|     selected_indices = {h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history}\\n 43|     available_indices = [i for i in candidate_indices if i not in selected_indices]\\n 44|     \\n 45|     # If no history (first round), use random selection with some diversity\\n 46|     if not history:\\n 47|         # Simple random sampling for the first batch\\n 48|         selected = rng.choice(available_indices, size=min(batch_size, len(available_indices)), replace=False)\\n 49|         return selected.tolist()\\n 50|     \\n 51|     # Build statistics from history\\n 52|     # Track mean score and count for each candidate\\n 53|     scores = {}\\n 54|     counts = {}\\n 55|     \\n 56|     for h in history:\\n 57|         idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n 58|         score = h[\'score\']\\n 59|         if idx not in scores:\\n 60|             scores[idx] = 0.0\\n 61|             counts[idx] = 0\\n 62|         scores[idx] += score\\n 63|         counts[idx] += 1\\n 64|     \\n 65|     # Calculate mean scores\\n 66|     mean_scores = {idx: scores[idx] / counts[idx] for idx in scores}\\n 67|     \\n 68|     # Calculate gene family bonuses based on historical extreme effects\\n 69|     # Genes from families with high absolute scores get a bonus\\n 70|     family_scores = {}\\n 71|     family_counts = {}\\n 72|     \\n 73|     for idx, score in mean_scores.items():\\n 74|         gene_name = candidates[idx].get(\'gene\', \'\')\\n 75|         # Extract gene family prefix (e.g., \\"ZNF\\" from \\"ZNF123\\", \\"ATP\\" from \\"ATP6V0D1\\")\\n 76|         family = gene_name.split(\'_\')[0]  # Handle cases like \\"ZNF816-ZNF321P\\"\\n 77|         # Take first part before any hyphen\\n 78|         family = family.split(\'-\')[0]\\n 79|         \\n 80|         if family not in family_scores:\\n 81|             family_scores[family] = 0.0\\n 82|             family_counts[family] = 0\\n 83|         family_scores[family] += abs(score)\\n 84|         family_counts[family] += 1\\n 85|     \\n 86|     # Calculate average absolute score per family\\n 87|     family_avg_abs = {}\\n 88|     for family in family_scores:\\n 89|         family_avg_abs[family] = family_scores[family] / family_counts[family]\\n 90|     \\n 91|     # UCB algorithm: balance mean reward vs exploration bonus vs family bonus\\n 92|     total_pulls = len(history)\\n 93|     ucb_scores = []\\n 94|     \\n 95|     for idx in available_indices:\\n 96|         gene_name = candidates[idx].get(\'gene\', \'\')\\n 97|         family = gene_name.split(\'_\')[0].split(\'-\')[0]\\n 98|         \\n 99|         if idx in mean_scores:\\n100|             # Exploitation term: absolute mean score (prioritize extreme effects)\\n101|             # Since hits are defined by large deviations in either direction\\n102|             exploitation = abs(mean_scores[idx])\\n103|             # Exploration term: uncertainty bonus with tuned constant and epsilon regularization\\n104|             # Use a slightly higher exploration constant (2.5 vs 2.0) to encourage more exploration\\n105|             # Add small epsilon to prevent division by zero and handle low-count candidates\\n106|             exploration = np.sqrt(2.5 * np.log(total_pulls + 1) / (counts[idx] + 1e-6))\\n107|             # Family bonus: prioritize genes from families with historically extreme effects\\n108|             # Weight: 0.3 * family_avg_abs (moderate influence, tuned empirically)\\n109|             family_bonus = 0.3 * family_avg_abs.get(family, 0.0)\\n110|             ucb = exploitation + exploration + family_bonus\\n111|         else:\\n112|             # Never-seen candidates get high priority for exploration\\n113|             # But also consider family bonus for never-seen candidates\\n114|             family_bonus = 0.3 * family_avg_abs.get(family, 0.0)\\n115|             ucb = float(\'inf\') + family_bonus\\n116|         ucb_scores.append((ucb, idx))\\n117|     \\n118|     # Sort by UCB score (descending) and select top candidates\\n119|     ucb_scores.sort(reverse=True)\\n120|     selected = [idx for _, idx in ucb_scores[:batch_size]]\\n121|     \\n122|     # If we don\'t have enough high-UCB candidates, fill with random unexplored ones\\n123|     if len(selected) < batch_size:\\n124|         remaining = [idx for idx in available_indices if idx not in selected]\\n125|         needed = batch_size - len(selected)\\n126|         if remaining:\\n127|             additional = rng.choice(remaining, size=min(needed, len(remaining)), replace=False)\\n128|             selected.extend(additional.tolist())\\n129|     \\n130|     return selected"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now let me check if there are any proposer reasoning files to understand the thought process:\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_8aa110577bb14dffaed8f443', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Carnevale22_Adenosine/run-2/candidates/candidate_4/proposer_reasoning.md"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_8aa110577bb14dffaed8f443', 'content': '{\n  "content": " 1| # Evolution Proposal - Candidate 4\\n 2| \\n 3| ## What Changed\\n 4| \\n 5| Added a **gene family clustering bonus** to the UCB selection algorithm. The model now:\\n 6| \\n 7| 1. **Extracts gene family prefixes** from gene names (e.g., \\"ZNF\\" from \\"ZNF123\\", \\"ATP\\" from \\"ATP6V0D1\\")\\n 8| 2. **Calculates average absolute scores** per family based on historical observations\\n 9| 3. **Adds a family bonus** (0.3 × family_avg_abs) to the UCB score for genes from families with extreme historical effects\\n10| \\n11| ## Why This Change\\n12| \\n13| **Key Observation:** Analysis of the top 15 hit genes revealed:\\n14| - ZNHIT2 (abs=1.360)\\n15| - ATP6V0D1 (abs=0.975)\\n16| - ZNF76 (abs=0.610)\\n17| - ZNF785 (abs=0.576)\\n18| - ZNG1A (abs=0.566)\\n19| - ZNF619 (abs=0.462)\\n20| - ZNF804A (abs=0.431)\\n21| - ZNF697 (abs=0.390)\\n22| - ZNF713 (abs=0.381)\\n23| - ZNG1C (abs=0.380)\\n24| - ZNF615 (abs=0.370)\\n25| - ZNF671 (abs=0.362)\\n26| \\n27| **Pattern:** 8 out of 15 top hits (53%) are ZNF (Zinc Finger) genes, and 2 are ZNG genes. This strong clustering suggests that:\\n28| - Genes from the same family may have similar functional effects\\n29| - Family-level signals can guide exploration more efficiently than pure UCB\\n30| \\n31| ## Expected Impact\\n32| \\n33| **Hypothesis:** By adding a family bonus, the algorithm will:\\n34| 1. **Prioritize exploration of promising gene families** (like ZNF, ZNG, ATP families)\\n35| 2. **Improve hit rate** by exploiting the biological clustering pattern\\n36| 3. **Maintain exploration** through the existing UCB mechanism\\n37| 4. **Achieve better scores** than the current best (27.77)\\n38| \\n39| **Conservative Tuning:** The family bonus weight (0.3) is moderate to avoid overfitting to the observed pattern while still providing meaningful guidance.\\n40| \\n41| ## Why This Is Better Than Prior Attempts\\n42| \\n43| - **Candidate 1 → 2:** Added `abs()` to handle extreme effects in both directions (fundamental improvement)\\n44| - **Candidate 2 → 3:** Tuned exploration constant (2.0 → 2.5) and added regularization (incremental improvement)\\n45| - **Candidate 3 → 4:** Leverages biological signal through family clustering (novel, data-driven improvement)\\n46| \\n47| This change goes beyond pure algorithmic tuning to exploit domain-specific patterns observed in the data."\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Perfect! Now I have a clear understanding of the evolution history. Let me analyze the patterns:\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Score Progression:**\n- Candidate 1: 22.37 (UCB baseline)\n- Candidate 2: 26.74 (added abs() for extreme effects)\n- Candidate 3: 27.77 (tuned exploration constant 2.0→2.5)\n- Candidate 4: 29.41 (added gene family bonus)\n\n**Key Observations:**\n1. All improvements have been incremental modifications to the UCB algorithm\n2. The family bonus in candidate 4 showed significant improvement (27.77→29.41)\n3. The recent strategy tags are [\'feature\', \'uncertainty\'] - referring to family features and UCB uncertainty exploration\n\n**Explore Mode Constraint:**\n- I need to try a "meaningfully different approach" \n- Must introduce at least one NEW strategy tag not in [\'feature\', \'uncertainty\']\n- Lookback window: last 10 candidates (we only have 4, so this is fine)\n\n**Novel Strategy Ideas:**\n- **Thompson Sampling** (probabilistic approach) - strategy tag: \'bayesian\'\n- **Genetic Algorithm** (evolutionary approach) - strategy tag: \'evolutionary\'  \n- **Gradient-based optimization** - strategy tag: \'gradient\'\n- **Clustering-based selection** - strategy tag: \'clustering\'\n\nLet me create a todo list and implement a Thompson Sampling approach, which is fundamentally different from UCB:\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_98b3d4b372b047e38557efce', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'write_todos', 'arguments': '{"todos": [{"description": "Copy current best model to candidate_5 directory", "status": "pending"}, {"description": "Implement Thompson Sampling with Beta-Bernoulli model for hit prediction", "status": "pending"}, {"description": "Write proposer_reasoning.md explaining the Thompson Sampling approach and novelty", "status": "pending"}]}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_98b3d4b372b047e38557efce', 'content': '{\n  "content": "Successfully updated the todo list. The current list is now:\\n1. [pending] Copy current best model to candidate_5 directory\\n2. [pending] Implement Thompson Sampling with Beta-Bernoulli model for hit prediction\\n3. [pending] Write proposer_reasoning.md explaining the Thompson Sampling approach and novelty"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_5cff5723cf6b4a17ab9ee56c', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'write_todos', 'arguments': '{"todos": [{"description": "Copy current best model to candidat